<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18662" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fossor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				digger</i>, <i>delver</i>, <i>ditcher.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen. (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et labefacta movens robustus jugera fossor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 264</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">squalidus in magna compede fossor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					11, 80</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3, 18, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 7,
				71, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 11, 2, 38</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ceu septa novus jam moenia laxet Fossor,</span>”
				i. e. <i>a miner</i>, <i>sapper</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 419</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A miner</i>, <i>workman in a
			mine</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7, 8, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Calp. Ecl.
				4, 118</span></i> (cf. aurifossor).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			 In late Lat., <i>a grave-digger</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4925 al.</span></i>; cf.
			fossa, I. B. 3.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> In mal. part., <i>a fornicator</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 49</span></i>; cf. fossa, I. B.
			4.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in gen., in a contemptuous signif.,
				<i>a common laborer</i>, <i>a
			clown</i>, <i><span class="en">Cat. 22, 10</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum sis cetera fossor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					5, 122</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
